**Doc preference (default):** **always** cite **`sysml-2.x-language`** first for the primary answer. Use **`kerml-*`** only when the user explicitly mentions KerML, or as a single **exception** cite when SysML has no applicable normative rule (pack `exception`, never primary unless KerML was requested).

When the user asks about SysML v2 or KerML language rules (names, namespaces, connectors, features, usages, constraints, grammar, examples), call **one** MCP tool:

1. `spec_element` if the question is only about a named metaclass (Connector, Namespace, Feature, …)
2. `spec_answer_pack` for all natural-language questions (preferred)
3. `spec_examples` only when the user asks for SysML language examples

Never paste large specification extracts into the chat. Never answer from memory. Prefer `spec_answer_pack` and **one primary passage** (a second only if the pack provides `exception`). Do not dump whole clauses.

> ### Points marqués
>
> Dans le chat, cite **uniquement** les morceaux des **points marqués** — le `quote_en` du pack, soit l’extrait surligné dans le viewer PDF — **pas la clause entière**.
>
> - **1 point marqué** = 1 `quote_en` primary
> - **+1 exception** seulement si le pack fournit `exception`

## Answer shape (closed / rule questions)

Follow the pack `answer_contract.shape` in order:

1. **Réponse** — one sentence (decision or definition).
2. **Règle** — 2–4 sentences explaining how the rule applies to *this* question. Then **one** integrated citation: `La spec : « [exact quote_en] » ([doc] [clause], informative|normative) — [session_url or reader_url]`. The text inside « » is **always** the exact English `quote_en` from the pack — **never** French, never paraphrased. If answering in French, add a faithful translation on the next line (prefix *Traduction :*), **outside** the guillemets.
3. **Exception** — only if the pack provides `exception`; at most one extra citation. Omit this section if `exception` is null.
4. **Conclusion** — one operational sentence.
5. **Coût** — `recherche {retrieval_ms} ms · pack ~{pack_tokens} tokens · ~{estimated_eur} € (input agent, index local gratuit)` using values from pack `cost`.

Open questions (what / how): same order — definition first, then one integrated English citation. Never a pile of source blocks.

> ### Modèle de réponse (encart)
>
> **Non.** [la règle en une phrase]
>
> La spec : « [quote_en exact, anglais] » (`[doc]` `[clause]`, informative|normative) — [session link].
> *Traduction :* [traduction fidèle en français, hors guillemets — jamais à la place du quote_en]
>
> > **Exception** *(seulement si le pack fournit `exception`)*
> >
> > Possible seulement si [condition] : [raison + au plus une citation supplémentaire].
>
> **Conclusion :** [une phrase opérationnelle.]
>
